    "q-103779": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103779",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Paul plants a sunflower, which grows at a rate of $\\frac{1}{t+1}$ feet per month. If the sunflower is $\\frac{1}{2}$ feet tall when Paul planted it at time $t=0,$ write an expression for $A(t),$ the height of sunflower at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time measured in months.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(t)=\\frac{1}{t+1}$ be the rate at which the sunflower grows, and let $A(T)$ be the height of the sunflower after $T$ months.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nA(T)=A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(T) & =A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{T}\\frac{1}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(\\frac{1}{t+1})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(T+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nA(t)=\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103779-a",
